  "content": {
    "id": "p18-p2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Solve the following for $x\\in[-\\pi,\\pi]$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-p2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^2x=\\sqrt3\\sin x\\cos x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac{5\\pi}{6},-\\frac\\pi2,\\frac\\pi6,\\frac\\pi2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos^2x-\\sqrt3\\sin x\\cos x&=0\\\\\\cos x(\\cos x-\\sqrt3\\sin x)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\cos x=0$, $x=-\\frac\\pi2,\\frac\\pi2$.\n\nFor the other factor,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos x&=\\sqrt3\\sin x\\\\\\tan x&=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $x=-\\frac{5\\pi}{6},\\frac\\pi6$. Together,\n$$x=-\\frac{5\\pi}{6},-\\frac\\pi2,\\frac\\pi6,\\frac\\pi2.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-p2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^2x-\\sin^2x=3\\sin x-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac\\pi6,\\frac{5\\pi}{6}$.",
          "worked": "Use $\\cos^2x=1-\\sin^2x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}1-2\\sin^2x&=3\\sin x-1\\\\2\\sin^2x+3\\sin x-2&=0\\\\(2\\sin x-1)(\\sin x+2)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\sin x=\\frac12$ or $\\sin x=-2$. Reject $-2$ because $-1\\leq\\sin x\\leq1$. In the given domain,\n$$x=\\frac\\pi6,\\frac{5\\pi}{6}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
